 "findings": [
  {
   "heading": "Overview",
   "segment_index": "S2.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:23-23",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.vn.qmd:23-23",
   "proposition": "The English says survival analysis is used in cancer epidemiology to assess a large variety of cancer survival measures; the Vietnamese says it is used to assess the survival status of a number of cancer treatment measures (\"danh gia tinh trang song con cua mot so cac bien phap dieu tri ung thu\"), dropping cancer epidemiology and turning survival measures into treatment methods.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader takes survival analysis to be a tool for evaluating cancer treatments, and does not learn that it underpins the routine survival measures (net survival, relative survival, RMST) produced in cancer epidemiology and registry work.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Load packages / Goi packages",
   "segment_index": "S4.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:45-45",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.vn.qmd:45-45",
   "proposition": "The English says survival is ONE OF the most widely used packages for survival analysis; the Vietnamese says survival is THE most widely used package (\"la goi lenh duoc su dung rong rai nhat\").",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader treats survival as the single dominant package and is less likely to look for the alternatives the English deliberately leaves room for.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Running initial analyses / Thuc hien cac phan tich ban dau",
   "segment_index": "S9.P1",
   "kind": "missing",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:257-257",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.vn.qmd:257-257",
   "proposition": "The English defines n.risk as people who have neither had the event yet NOR been censored; the Vietnamese parenthesis reads \"nguoi chua co su kien cung nhu su kien chua xay ra\", which repeats the no-event condition twice and omits the censoring condition entirely.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader learns an incomplete definition of the risk set and may believe censored individuals stay in n.risk after they leave follow-up, which mis-reads every life table printed in this chapter.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Log rank test / Kiem dinh Log rank",
   "segment_index": "S13.P4",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:426-426",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.vn.qmd:426-426",
   "proposition": "The English CAUTION says survminer functions need the data USED TO FIT the survival object to be specified again; the Vietnamese says to specify the dataset \"de so sanh doi tuong song sot\" (to compare the survival object).",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader does not learn that the data argument must be the same data the survfit object was fitted on, and may pass a different dataset, producing the non-specific error message the caution exists to prevent.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Fitting a Cox model / Fitting mot mo hinh Cox",
   "segment_index": "S15.P3",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:544-544",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.vn.qmd:544-544",
   "proposition": "The English NOTE says the method argument determines how TIES are handled; the Vietnamese says it determines how \"rang buoc\" (constraints) are applied.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader does not learn that method controls the tied-event-time approximation, so cannot judge when efron, breslow or exact matters, and may look for a constraint feature that coxph() does not have.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Fitting a Cox model / Fitting mot mo hinh Cox",
   "segment_index": "S15.P7",
   "kind": "missing",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:597-597",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.vn.qmd:597-597",
   "proposition": "The English explanation is that patients WHO LIVE LONG ENOUGH to be admitted later had less severe disease to begin with; the Vietnamese drops the surviving-long-enough clause and states only that patients admitted later had less severe disease at the start.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader misses the survivor-selection mechanism behind the apparent protective effect of later admission, and reads the association as a plain severity effect rather than as a bias to be investigated.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  }
 ]
}